<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuvan People's Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tuvan People's Revolutionary Party was the ruling communist party of the Tuvan People's Republic, the Soviet-backed state in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>. From 1932 its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salchak-toka">Salchak Toka</a> imposed a Stalinist regime, collectivising herds, closing Buddhist monasteries and persecuting lamas. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuva">Tuva</a> was annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1944, the party was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Communist Party of the Soviet Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuvan-peoples-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="Tuvan People's Revolutionary Party" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TheSign 1998 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Tuvinian_Peoples_Revolutionary_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
